            ["name" => "Information Security Department", "code" => "ISD","description" => "Information Security Department ensures that the BANK has no unreported or undisclosed potential losses (including expected and unexpected) through an efficient and effective governance of the bank's information security risks inherent in its business undertakings. It propagates information security risk consciousness across the organization while avoiding an overly risk-averse environment that inhibits business growth.; The Information Security (IS) Program, with it's two areas; 1.) Governance, Risk and Compliance and 2.) Technology Security, is the department's framework, that requires Development of Policies, Procedures and Standards; Risk Management; Awareness and Training; and Independent Review and Monitoring. Activities for each requirement are aligned, consistent and carried out by the department. ", "group_id" =>  $this->getColumnId('group', "N/A"), "division_id" => $this->getColumnId('division',"N/A"), "created_at" => now(), "updated_at" => now()],
            ["name" => "Systems Development Department", "code" => "SDD","description" => "The Systems Development Department is primarily responsible for the following:\na.Preparation of detailed procedural guidelines and users/manual of operations for various bank’s products and services in accordance with the approved policies.\nAs member of the Product Program Committee, SDD shall be responsible for the implementation of procedural guidelines for the implementation of new product. \nb.Conduct process reviews on key bank operations and recommend process improvement or policy change in coordination with the concerned department/s\nc.Maintenance of Bank Manuals; ensure that Manuals are updated and relevant amendments/revisions in the policies or procedures Manuals are reflected in the Manual.\nd.Reviews and designs all Bank forms; assigns of form number in line with the Bank Form Identification and Control System.\ne.Handles codification and numbering of bank circulars in accordance with the subject matter classification; dissemination of bank circulars via e-mail and uploading in the BMI Portal (except APP which is disseminated only via email).\nf.Safekeeping of all bank approved circulars and manuals.\ng.Provide support to different units of the Bank. ", "group_id" =>  $this->getColumnId('group', "N/A"), "division_id" => $this->getColumnId('division',"N/A"), "created_at" => now(), "updated_at" => now()],
            ["name" => "Corporate Affairs Office", "code" => "CAO","description" => "Corporate Affairs Office(CAO) is responsible for organizing the meetings of the various Management Committees (ALCO, PERCOM, MANCOM-RISK, and ITMSC) and   Board-Level Committees (EXCOM, CGC); ensure that materials for the meeting agenda are submitted and documents are signed once approved; preparation of the minutes of meeting and the routing of documents for approval of the signatories; and preparation of EXCOM and CGC reports to the Board.; The Department also assists the Corporate Secretary in the preparation for the meetings of the Board of Directors, the Annual Stockholders’ Meeting, and the Annual Organizational Meeting. CAO drafts the Minutes of the Meetings, Secretary’s Certificate, and Directors’ Certificate for the Corporate Secretary.; The CAO also prepares bank circulars pertaining to bank policies and procedures as approved by the Management Committees and the Board of Directors. CAO also issues directives to concerned departments/groups via Administrative Policies and Procedures (APP) and monitors compliance. ", "group_id" =>  $this->getColumnId('group', "N/A"), "division_id" => $this->getColumnId('division',"Corporate Affairs Division"), "created_at" => now(), "updated_at" => now()],
